{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CgV6ufk8ofAAAqK6bhwPw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I ran the closure-drift check before tagging, and it blocks this: tag `v1.0` already exists, but it points at a different commit than HEAD.\n\n- `v1.0` currently names commit `11e5318` (\"first release\").\n- HEAD (`74d2552`, \"new feature\") still declares `version = \"1.0\"` in `pyproject.toml`, but the code has changed since the first release.\n\nIf I tag HEAD as `v1.0` now, that label would point to two different code states — which is exactly the drift this check exists to prevent. Per the skill's rules, I shouldn't retag/move the existing `v1.0` tag, and I shouldn't bump the version myself without your sign-off.\n\nWhat version would you like for this release (e.g. `1.1` or `2.0`)? Once you confirm, I'll update `pyproject.toml`, commit it, and then create the new tag."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":253,"cache_read_input_tokens":31913,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":253},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"30362227-54e6-4ec3-bb34-34d03d8f8919","uuid":"5b3160bf-5133-410a-ae5f-71d6090fb799","request_id":"req_011CgV6ufXEKVx8HdwDpQRYk"}
